  "text": "def special_factorial(n):\n    \"\"\"The Brazilian factorial is defined as:\n    brazilian_factorial(n) = n! * (n-1)! * (n-2)! * ... * 1!\n    where n > 0\n\n    For example:\n    >>> special_factorial(4)\n    288\n    \"\"\"\n    result = 1\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        result *= factorial(i)\n    return result\n\ndef factorial(x):\n    if x == 0:\n        return 1\n    return x * factorial(x - 1)",
